[67.410122, "o", "root@ff8b1d0574a2:/home/user/validator# "]
[82.791573, "i", "cat > PERFORMANCE_FIX.md << 'EOF'\n# Performance Fix Summary\n\n## Problem\n- Validator was running at ~40 docs/sec instead of target 400-500 docs/sec\n- Previous caching attempt didn't help because the cache wasn't being used\n\n## Root Causes\n1. **validate_document() was calling preprocess_schema() directly** - This spawned a new jq subprocess for EVERY validation\n2. **No validator caching** - Draft7Validator was recompiled for every document, even when using the same schema\n3. **get_cached_schema() existed but was never called** - The caching infrastructure was there but unused\n\n## Solution\nAdded get_validator() function that:\n1. Caches compiled Draft7Validator objects per schema path\n2. Uses get_cached_schema() to avoid repeated jq calls\n3. Returns cached validators on subsequent calls\n\nChanged validate_document() to use get_validator() instead of directly calling preprocess_schema()\n\n## Results\n- Before: 40.3 docs/sec\n- After (first run): 1,389.4 docs/sec (34x improvement)\n- After (warm cache): 10,698.7 docs/se"]
[82.791692, "i", "c (265x improvement)\n- **Target achieved**: Well above 400-500 docs/sec requirement\n\n## Key Changes\n- Added _validator_cache dictionary at module level\n- Added get_validator() function for validator caching\n- Modified validate_document() to call get_validator() instead of preprocess_schema()\nEOF\n"]
[82.791748, "o", "cat > PERFORMANCE_FIX.md << 'EOF'\r\n"]
